      ],
      "source": "https://pequeatwp.org/history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1877, Frederick Shoff and Paul Heine turned the area into a resort town after the Columbia and Port Deposit Railroad began carrying passengers there.",
